msgid "This domain is routed through the naulon fleet, which is already collecting the toll for it. Turning on in-app enforcement as well would charge an agent twice for the same read, so it stays off. To run the toll from WordPress instead, remove the naulon CNAME record for this domain at your DNS provider, wait for it to stop resolving, then run this step again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:165
msgid "This site is already verified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:197
msgid "Challenge ready. This site is now serving the proof."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:220
msgid "Ownership verified. This site can now settle tolls."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:251
msgid "This site is served over http. The ownership check is https-only, so it can never succeed until the site has a certificate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:257
msgid "No challenge is open. Start verification first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: transport error message.
#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:266
#, php-format
msgid "This site could not fetch its own challenge URL (%s). That is usually a firewall or a loopback restriction on the host, not a naulon problem — but the control plane may hit the same wall."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: HTTP status, 2: redirect target.
#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:272
#, php-format
msgid "The challenge URL answers %1$d and redirects to %2$s. Redirects are never followed by the checker, so verification must run against the host that actually serves the page — usually the www or non-www variant you were not expecting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:274
msgid "another address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:277
msgid "The challenge URL returns 404. Something is intercepting /.well-known/ — commonly a security plugin, a static-file handler, or stale permalinks. Re-saving Settings → Permalinks fixes the stale case; the meta-tag method sidesteps the interception entirely."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: HTTP status code.
#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:281
#, php-format
msgid "The challenge URL returns %d. The checker only accepts a 2xx."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the first bytes actually returned.
#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:287
#, php-format
msgid "The challenge URL answered 200 but the body was not the token. It returned: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:300
msgid "This site is serving the challenge correctly from here, so WordPress is doing its part. If the check still fails, something between the checker and this server is answering instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:301
msgid "If a CDN or firewall sits in front of this site — Cloudflare, a security service, your host's WAF — allow the path /.well-known/naulon-challenge/ through it. The checker is a plain server-to-server request with no browser behind it, which bot protection is built to challenge, and a challenge page is not the token."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:302
msgid "Otherwise the checker is reaching a different machine than this one: a staging copy, or DNS pointing somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:349
msgid "No challenge is open for this host. Start verification again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:351
msgid "The DNS TXT record does not match yet. DNS changes can take a while to propagate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:353
msgid "Another account already verified this domain. If that was you, connect this site with that account's key instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:355
msgid "The control plane could not see the proof yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:368
msgid "The control plane rejected this API key (401). It may have been revoked or mistyped. Nothing is being tolled until this is fixed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:380
msgid "This site is already verified, so the setup key has handed its domain permission back — it only ever needed it once. To claim a domain from here again, open your naulon dashboard, go to Settings → API & webhooks → Create key, choose \"Connect WordPress\", and paste the new key on this page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-verification.php:382
msgid "This key cannot claim domains (403). In your naulon dashboard go to Settings → API & webhooks → Create key and choose \"Connect WordPress\" — that preset is the only one that mints the permission this step needs. A key built from the permission list is read-only and can never prove this domain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-wallet.php:72
msgid "Enter a wallet address, or leave this empty — your posts will simply read free."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-wallet.php:76
msgid "A wallet address starts with 0x."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-wallet.php:79
msgid "A wallet address is 42 characters: 0x followed by 40 hex digits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-wallet.php:82
msgid "That address contains characters that are not hex digits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-naulon-wallet.php:85
msgid "That is the burn address — anything sent there is destroyed. Use the wallet you actually control."
msgstr ""
